Fixed in round 53 (the V1/V2 arc's first correctness increment): while a
specialization is instantiated, a sibling/enclosing instantiation's
same-spelled parameter bindings are hidden ([temp.point]/1 +
[basic.scope.temp]/2), so apply()'s short-name bridge cannot pick the
wrong instance's binding.  Kernel runtime-verified with clang++.
